<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">1989 Tiananmen Square protests and massacre</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1989</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Tiananmen Square massacre, 1989 Tiananmen Square protests, Tiananmen Square protests</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The 1989 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiananmen">Tiananmen</a> Square protests were student-led demonstrations in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> and other Chinese cities from April to June 1989, calling for political reform, freedom of the press and an end to corruption. The government declared martial law, and on the night of 3–4 June the army cleared Tiananmen Square and the surrounding streets, killing hundreds and possibly thousands of people.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/1989-tiananmen-square-protests-and-massacre.jpg" alt="1989 Tiananmen Square protests and massacre" width="299" height="199" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jiří Tondl (Blow up) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ud%C3%A1losti_na_n%C3%A1m%C4%9Bst%C3%AD_Tian_an_men,_%C4%8C%C3%ADna_1989,_foto_Ji%C5%99%C3%AD_Tondl.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
